-- title:
--   Fibre-model independence of the specialisation of places
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N$, a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $\ell$, and a surjective ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$. Let $fm_1$ and $fm_2$ be two terms of type `FibreModel N A ℓ k red`, that is, each consists of subrings $B_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, $B_{\infty}$ of the base-changed field `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull N)` containing the constants $\mathrm{im}(A)$, with $\bar\jmath$ and $\bar\jmath_N$ in $B_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ and $\bar\jmath^{-1}$ in $B_{\infty}$, both integral over the respective subrings `affineBaseFin N A`, `affineBaseInf N A` generated by the constants together with $\bar\jmath$ resp. $\bar\jmath^{-1}$, together with ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{Fin}}, \pi_{\infty}$ to `modularFunctionFieldC k N` = $k(j, j_N)$ inside the Laurent series over $k$, which induce $red$ on constants and send $\bar\jmath, \bar\jmath_N$ resp. $\bar\jmath^{-1}$ to their characteristic-$\ell$ counterparts (plus the remaining clauses of the structure). Assume further that each of $fm_1$, $fm_2$ carries a cusp chart, i.e. $\bar\jmath_N\,\bar\jmath^{-N}$ lies in $B_{\infty}$ and $\pi_{\infty}$ sends it to $j_N j^{-N}$. Let $dataAll$ assign to every divisor $d \mid N$ a modular polynomial datum (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(d)$ in $Y$ vanishing at $(j, j_d)$), and assume the level-$N$ polynomial, reduced mod $\ell$ and viewed over $k(X)$, is separable. Then the two induced maps on places, $fm_1.\mathrm{spPlace}$ and $fm_2.\mathrm{spPlace}$, from places of `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull N)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` over $k$, are equal.
--
--   This is the statement that the specialisation of places from the characteristic-zero function field of $X_0(N)$ to its characteristic-$\ell$ counterpart depends only on the reduction datum $red : A \to k$ and not on the chosen fibre model; it extends [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_eq), which treats the residue field of $A$ with its canonical reduction, to an arbitrary field $k$ equipped with a surjective reduction map. It is used in the analysis of prolongation tuples, where saturation of the residue at a node is deduced from the agreement of a specialisation with the one coming from the residue field.
